          "evidence": "Authored module notes: Captures Spyder's primary INI preferences (%APPDATA%\\spyder-py3\\config\\spyder.ini): editor, font, keybindings, appearance, and run configurations. Logs, autosave, history, LSP logs, and completion caches are excluded. Sensitivity is none for local-only setups; secrets block guards against users who configure remote kernels with tokens. Confidence: high - config path confirmed by Spyder documentation and %APPDATA%\\spyder-py3 is the canonical Windows config root. Authored secret warning: spyder.ini may embed remote kernel connection info (e.g. SSH tunnels, remote Jupyter server URLs and tokens). Review the captured file before sharing a bundle. Authored excluded secret or machine-bound paths: %APPDATA%\\spyder-py3\\config\\spyder.ini"
